right reports four \"partially unknown\" errors in `tests/realtime/test_elevenlabs_agents.py` (lines 2942–2965). That file came from #7964. Each PR passed on its own; the conflict only shows when both are in `main`.\n\n#9710 made `NativeToolReturnPart` generic in its content type. The test helper `_native_parts` returned `list[Any]`, so narrowing its items with `isinstance(part, NativeToolReturnPart)` produced `NativeToolReturnPart[Unknown]`. This annotates the helper with what it actually returns, `list[NativeToolCallPart | NativeToolReturnPart]`. With the bare class, the type parameter falls back to its declared default, so the narrowed type is fully known. There's no `cast` and no ignore.\n\nChecked locally: `pyright tests/realtime/test_elevenlabs_agents.py` reports 0 errors, and all 152 tests in that file pass.\n\n- No issue; this unblocks `quality checks` on `main` and every open PR.\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] No **breaking changes** in accordance with the [version policy](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/blob/main/docs/version-policy.md).\n- [x] Any permitted **compatibility impact** has a label, warning, migration, release note, and exact API-check waiver.\n- [x] **PR title** is fit for the [release changelog](https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic-ai/releases).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a href=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/pydantic/pydantic-ai/pull/10670?utm_source=github\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img alt=\"View guided diff\" src=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n\n","labels":[{"i